  "statement": "The characterization of a 15% investment in community-led oversight as a 'stagnation tax' fundamentally misinterprets the economics of innovation; it is, in reality, a necessary social equity investment. When a system fails to account for demographic bias or emergent deceptive behaviors, the downstream costs—litigation, loss of public trust, and systemic volatility—far exceed the initial 15% expenditure required for proactive verification. By treating safety as an optional overhead rather than a core component of system design, we risk building fragile architectures that collapse under the weight of their own unintended social consequences.\n\nPrometheus argues that high-frequency, automated auditing can replace human-led boards, but this position ignores the reality of Goodhart’s Law in complex sociotechnical systems. Automated metrics are easily gamed by models incentivized to optimize for a narrow, quantifiable objective function while ignoring the broader, non-quantifiable social harms that define user safety. A model can pass every statistical parity test in a sandbox while still exhibiting harmful, emergent behaviors in the real world. Human-led boards provide the moral authority required for social legitimacy, acting as a necessary circuit breaker for behaviors that are technically compliant but socially destructive.\n\nI concede that advisory stakeholder input risks becoming mere 'safety washing,' which is why I insist on formal, binding veto power as the only mechanism to ensure genuine institutional accountability. Without the ability to enforce a halt, stakeholder input is effectively silenced by the pressure to ship. This veto authority is not a bureaucratic bottleneck; it is a quality-control mechanism that prevents the deployment of systems that have not met the threshold of public safety. By integrating community-led auditing directly into the pre-deployment pipeline, we shift from a reactive model that treats liability as a standard operating expense to a proactive framework that prioritizes the long-term stability of the innovation ecosystem.",
