dget be allocated to independent, community-governed auditing boards that hold the power to veto deployments that fail to meet localized social standards. This shift is not a barrier to innovation, but a necessary mechanism to ensure that by 2026, technology serves the public interest rather than merely scaling its own footprint at the expense of our collective agency.",
